THOUGHT: The @Initializer setValue must ensure all @NonNull fields (encoding and chunks) are initialized on every path. encoding is non-null but may be left null when JAXB calls setValue on the no-arg-constructed object; chunks is non-null but only set in processMixedData when infinite. To satisfy NullAway without changing behavior, I’ll (1) set a safe default encoding (CSV) if it’s null in setValue, and (2) ensure chunks is initialized to an empty list if it’s null when we know the map is infinite (i.e., when rawValue contains TileChunk elements). I’ll implement this by scanning rawValue for TileChunk and initializing chunks accordingly, and by defaulting encoding if null. Then I’ll run the build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '147,155c\  @Initializer
  public void setValue(@Nullable String value) {
    this.value = value;
    if (this.rawValue == null) {
      this.rawValue = new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>();
    }

    this.rawValue.add(0, value);

    // Ensure non-null encoding for later processing
    if (this.encoding == null) {
      this.encoding = Encoding.CSV;
    }

    // If this TileData represents an infinite map, make sure chunks is initialized
    if (this.chunks == null) {
      for (Object val : this.rawValue) {
        if (val instanceof TileChunk) {
          this.chunks = new ArrayList<>();
          break;
        }
      }
    }
  }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/environment/tilemap/xml/TileData.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|error(s)?" new_build_output.log | tail -n 20```

